[Music]  whether it's a dog cat or another animal  the bond we have with our pets is strong  and it's why for many the end of their  life can be as devastating as losing a  family member a young woman who knows  that loss is helping others with a  unique and inspiring gift janet shamley  had met up with her along the coast of  maine  just give them some love  kim kempton has hundreds of photos of  her boxer boone that's wonderful  hi  puppy that's a good boy  but these are the ones she'll treasure  forever we'll see if he says good balls  he's my child he's my baby  perhaps for only a few weeks more  boone is terminally ill  how hard do you think it'll be to let go  i try not to think about it  because i don't  remember what life was before him  lauren smith kennedy who just met kim is  taking the photos for free go ahead and  put your hand up to the side of yeah  just like that and then yeah that's  gorgeous just as she has for dozens of  other pet owners over the past year  grappling with the heartbreak of a  relationship coming to a close  you want to capture those last moments  whether they're happy whether they're  sad just for what they are because that  captures the true love you know that  captures the vulnerability the love the  commitment  the friendship all of that the first  time was a four-year-old pup named lacey  who had cancer  kennedy documented it in this tick tock  video grabbing the attention of more  than 650 000 people these are the photos  she gave to lacey's family when she  posted them on social media and offered  to do the same for others with pets  whose time was running short the  floodgates opened  how quickly did this explode for you  like where were people coming from yeah  families from california from out of the  state from canada you know all asking if  they could travel to me or if i would  fly to them to be able to do this so the  outreach was absolutely incredible in a  matter of weeks in a matter of days days  [Applause]  already working two jobs lauren filled  with little free time she had taking  photos like these thousands were  commenting on them hundreds reaching out  some offering to fly her cross-country  to do the same for them  so you quickly realize like that was not  a reality absolutely i was only one  person this was during the height of  kovid so that's when you know i started  getting other photographers commenting  on it saying if anyone needs anything i  mean take my name you know i didn't know  this existed i'm so inspired let me give  you my name the 28 year old created this  website now with the names of more than  700 photographers worldwide willing to  take the end-of-life pet photos many  saying they'd also do it for free  it's called the chili project named for  the cat kennedy loved and then lost  she was the love of my life my best  friend in the entire world my soul mate  everything good in this world she was  just my sunshine and because i know that  grief that  heartbreaking life-stopping  just  earth-shattering grief  i know that these photographs can mean  so much to people and that's all i want  this is 13 year old tessa who had heart  disease and impaired hearing  but still loved a day at the beach  she just likes to be pet everywhere yeah  for her family susie and mark amid  sadness oh you're getting a hairdo  aren't you finding joy  i just have to keep trying to hold the  beauty part of 13 plus years of memories  that we have with you right bud  these photos will help them remember  sadly tessa passed away not long after  they were taken  and these are the photos kim kempton  will cherish of boone  this is just such a wonderful  opportunity  to capture him  with us  and the love that we share with him  for the animals we love whose lives are  never long enough the gift of  celebrating an unbreakable bond  it's a snapshot of time it's a snapshot  of that true emotions that you can have  forever that you can look back and say  i was feeling absolutely heartbreaking  but man was that a capture of my love  for cbs saturday morning janet chamleon  portland maine  beautiful just gorgeous and the memories  of just even the photo shoot itself  i'm sure just  helped them to grieve through it and  it's such a traumatizing and terrible  time for people as they go through this  to be able to have something and that  that mindset of let's treasure these  last moments too is very powerful it's  incredible as she said i mean i don't  remember what life was like before boone  and so she wants these final memories  beautiful piece janet thank you

